Package: usRds
Type: Package
Title: Load, Label and Analyze United States Renal Data System Files
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    c(
        person("Vagish", "Hemmige", email = "vagish.hemmige@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
               comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0006-6346-1826")),
        person("Miguel", "Cervera Hernandez", email = "Miguel.Cerverahernandez@SanfordHealth.org", role = "ctb")
    )
Description: Load, label and analyze files from the United States Renal
    Data System (USRDS), the national data system on chronic kidney disease
    and end-stage kidney disease in the United States. Users supply USRDS
    files they have obtained, in 'SAS', comma-separated values (CSV) or
    'Parquet' format; the package finds them, chooses one file for each file
    name and year, and reads them with upper-case column names. Variables and
    values can be labelled from the appendices of the USRDS Researcher's
    Guide. Medicare claims can be extracted by diagnosis, procedure and
    provider specialty codes, and used to date diagnoses, build cohorts, and
    compute claim costs with daily proration and medical care inflation
    adjustment.
